Author: Seth Junot <xsetech@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Feb 15 23:00:31 2026 -0800

    Fix protobuf header conflict with system protobuf on macOS

    On macOS with Homebrew, the OpenMP detection adds -I/usr/local/include
    to compiler flags. Since -I paths are searched before -isystem paths,
    this causes the system protobuf v33 headers (which no longer define
    PROTOBUF_VERSION) to shadow the bundled protobuf v3.13 headers,
    triggering a version mismatch error when compiling ONNX .pb.h files.

    Change include_directories from BEFORE SYSTEM to BEFORE so the bundled
    protobuf headers use -I instead of -isystem, giving them proper
    precedence.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/cmake/ProtoBuf.cmake b/cmake/ProtoBuf.cmake
index fe3113205df..54c68d083bc 100644
--- a/cmake/ProtoBuf.cmake
+++ b/cmake/ProtoBuf.cmake
@@ -107,7 +107,11 @@ endif()

 get_target_property(__tmp protobuf::libprotobuf INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES)
 message(STATUS "Caffe2 protobuf include directory: " ${__tmp})
-include_directories(BEFORE SYSTEM ${__tmp})
+# Use BEFORE without SYSTEM so that the bundled protobuf headers are added as
+# -I (not -isystem) includes. This ensures they take precedence over any system
+# protobuf headers that may be pulled in via broad -I paths (e.g.
+# -I/usr/local/include added by OpenMP detection on macOS).
+include_directories(BEFORE ${__tmp})

 # If Protobuf_VERSION is known (true in most cases, false if we are building
 # local protobuf), then we will add a protobuf version check in
